    {
      "fact": "Durham County Council publishes recommended dates; aided schools and academies can set different dates.",
      "source": "https://www.durham.gov.uk/schoolholidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Both 2026-27 and 2027-28 have 195 days, and schools use up to five of them for teacher training, known locally as PD days.",
      "source": "https://www.durham.gov.uk/schoolholidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "In 2025-26 the year had 193 days, with three PD days in term time and two more taken in the holidays or as twilight sessions.",
      "source": "https://www.durham.gov.uk/schoolholidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The council lists the May Day bank holiday as a short break: schools close on Friday 30 April and re-open on Tuesday 4 May 2027.",
      "source": "https://www.durham.gov.uk/schoolholidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The 2027-28 year starts on Wednesday 1 September 2027 and ends on Thursday 20 July 2028.",
      "source": "https://www.durham.gov.uk/schoolholidays"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The council says PD day dates are decided by each school and can often change, so parents should check the school website.",
      "source": "https://www.durham.gov.uk/schoolholidays"
    }
  ],
